bel":"Choose digits and split around the peak","methodDirectNodeIds":{"count-by-length":["cnm_h239","cnm_h231","cnm_h240"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h239","cnm_h231","cnm_h240"]},{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"choose-digits-and-sides","label":"Choose digits and their sides","methodDirectNodeIds":{"choose-digits-and-sides":["math:bijective-counting","cnm_h239","cnm_h231","cnm_h240"]},"nodeIds":["math:bijective-counting","cnm_h239","cnm_h231","cnm_h240"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"alignmentIds":["alignment:a5169760c44ddad1c2987dd0"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C: 9841","reason":"Fix the largest digit m. Every smaller digit is either unused, placed to the left in increasing order, or placed to the right in decreasing order. These choices give exactly 3^(m-1) fair integers. Summing over m = 1 through 9 gives 1+3+...+3^8 = (3^9-1)/2 = 9841. Equivalently, counting by length gives sum C(9,n)*2^(n-1).","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h240"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2025_AMC_12A_Q23","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"condition-on-number-length","label":"Count by length","methodDirectNodeIds":{"condition-on-number-length":["cnm_h239","cnm_h231","cnm_h240"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h239","cnm_h231","cnm_h240"]},{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"choose-digits-and-sides","label":"Choose digits and their sides","methodDirectNodeIds":{"choose-digits-and-sides":["math:bijective-counting","cnm_h239","cnm_h231","cnm_h240"]},"nodeIds":["math:bijective-counting","cnm_h239","cnm_h231","cnm_h240"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:a5169760c44ddad1c2987dd0"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: 1,008,016","reason":"Only even total degrees j in y and z survive. Each such degree contributes j+1 monomials with nonzero coefficients. The count is ∑ from k=0 to 1003 of (2k+1)=1004²=1,008,016.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h240"],"c