onalConceptCount":2,"alignmentIds":["alignment:a5169760c44ddad1c2987dd0"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E: 8","reason":"The binomial expansion gives (1.0025)^10 = 1.02528313... . Rounded to five decimal places this is 1.02528, whose fifth decimal digit is 8.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h240"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1971_AMC_12_Q13","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"binomial-expansion","label":"Expand around 1","methodDirectNodeIds":{"binomial-expansion":["cnm_023","cnm_h240","cnm_h242"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h240","cnm_023","cnm_h242"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"alignmentIds":["alignment:a5169760c44ddad1c2987dd0"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E: 1","reason":"Let the two cube roots be u and v. Then uv=-3 and u³+v³=10. For t=u+v, t³+9t-10=0, or (t-1)(t²+t+10)=0. The quadratic has negative discriminant, so t=1, which is not listed.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h240"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1980_AMC_12_Q27","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"recognize-conjugate-cubes","label":"Recognize conjugate cubes","methodDirectNodeIds":{"recognize-conjugate-cubes":["cnm_h240","cnm_173"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h240","cnm_173"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"alignmentIds":["alignment:a5169760c44ddad1c2987dd0"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 9","reason":"Let α=15+√220, β=15-√220, and S_n=α^n+β^n. Then S_n=30S_(n-1)-5S_(n-2), with S_1=30 and S_2=890, so every S_n for n≥1 is an integer divisible by 10. Since 0<β^19+β^82<1, the requested number has integer part S_19+S_82-1, ending in 9.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h240"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1982_AMC_12_Q30","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"conjugate-binomial-expansion","label":"Cancel radical terms by binomial expansion","methodDirectNodeIds":{"conjugate-binomial-expansion":["cnm_h240"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h240"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_079","cnm_p153","cnm_143"],"id":"binomial-conjugate-cancellation","label":"Cancel the radicals by binomial expansion","methodDirectNodeIds":{"binomial-conjugate-cancellation":["cnm_h240","math:modular-congruence","math:floor-ceiling"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h240","math:modular-congruence","math:floor-ceiling","cnm_079","cnm_p153","cnm_143"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"alignmentIds":["alignment:a5169760c44ddad1c2987dd0"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, (1+3^(-50))/2","reason":"If E and O are the even and odd probabilities, then E+O=1 and E-O=(1/3-2/3)^50=3^(-50). Therefore E=(1+3^(-50))/2.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h240"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":["Uses the standard independent-toss model with the same heads probability 2/3 on every toss."],"questionId":"1992_AMC_12_Q29","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"id":"binomial-parity-sum","label":"Sum even binomial terms","nodeIds":["cnm_h255","cnm_h240"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_h254","cnm_h140","cnm_h139","cnm_h236"],"id":"solution:binomial-parity-sum:f044245d694c","label":"Cancel the odd binomial terms","methodDirectNodeIds":{"binomial-parity-sum":["cnm_h255","cnm_h240","cnm_h138"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h255","cnm_h240","cnm_h138","cnm_h254","cnm_h140","cnm_h139","cnm_h236"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"alignmentIds":["alignment:a5169760c44ddad1c2987dd0"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B: √2−1","reason":"Each averaging step multiplies the leading term of the geometric progression by (1+x)/2. Therefore ((1+x)/2)¹⁰⁰=2⁻⁵⁰. Since x>0, taking positive roots gives 1+x=√2 and x=√2−1.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h240"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2006_AMC_12A_Q23","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","